Integers : All the natural numbers, zero, and the the negatives of natural numbers are called integers.
I = {......, -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, ......}
(i) Set of negative integers = {-1, -2, -3, ......}
(ii) Set of non-negative integers = {0, 1, 2, 3...}
(iii) Set of positive integers = {1, 2, 3 ......}
(iv) Set of non-positive integers = {0, 1, 2, 3......}
Note: '0' is definately a non-negative integer as well as a non-positive integer.
